<div class="container"><header class="page-heading"><span class="eyebrow">YOUR INFORMATION</span><h1>Project enquiry privacy.</h1><p>A straightforward explanation of what happens when you get in touch.</p></header><article class="prose listing-section"><h2>What you share</h2><p>The enquiry form collects your name, contact information, optional company details and project requirements. Please share only what is needed for an initial project discussion.</p><h2>Why it is collected</h2><p>Krunal Pawar uses these details to review your enquiry, respond through your preferred contact method and discuss a potential software development project. Submitting an enquiry does not subscribe you to marketing messages.</p><h2>Storage and notifications</h2><p>Enquiries are stored in a private application database. A notification may also be sent to the developer’s email account. Hosting and email providers process this information as needed to operate those services.</p><h2>Essential session data</h2><p>The contact form and content manager use an essential session cookie for request protection and sign-in. The site does not include advertising trackers. Short-lived, hashed network identifiers are used to limit automated form abuse.</p><h2>Questions and deletion requests</h2><p>To ask about your enquiry information or request its deletion, contact <a href="mailto:<?=e($config['email'])?>"><?=e($config['email'])?></a>. Information needed for an active project may be handled under the separate arrangements agreed for that work.</p></article></div>
